title: new_object silently discards apiVersion passed in the params hash -- inflate
  honours it
updated: 2026-08-31T19:04:11Z
---

new_object() takes the exact-GVK request only as its third positional
argument. An apiVersion INSIDE the params hashref is silently overwritten
with the version of whatever class the short name resolves to, while
inflate() reads the very same key and honours it.

Repro (measured, with IO::K8s::AgentSandbox loaded, post-karr #58):

  new_object("Sandbox", { apiVersion => "agents.x-k8s.io/v1alpha1", ... })
    --> IO::K8s::AgentSandbox::V1beta1::Sandbox
        api_version = agents.x-k8s.io/v1beta1     # caller ignored

  inflate({ kind => "Sandbox", apiVersion => "agents.x-k8s.io/v1alpha1", ... })
    --> IO::K8s::AgentSandbox::V1alpha1::Sandbox
        api_version = agents.x-k8s.io/v1alpha1    # caller honoured

Two entry points, same input key, opposite semantics, no diagnostic either
way. Not AgentSandbox-specific: it hits every kind that ships more than one
served version. The caller gets an object for a version they did not ask
for and only finds out at the API server (or not at all, when both versions
accept the payload).

Decision needed: either honour apiVersion from the params hash (symmetric
with inflate), or reject/warn when it contradicts the resolved class --
fail-closed is the house line (karr #37/#39). Silently substituting a
different API version is the one option that should not survive.

Found by the sandbox lane while implementing karr #58 (repro verified by
the orchestrating agent).
Lane: decision first, then io-k8s-worker.

2026-08-31 03:42 Decision: honour params-hash apiVersion (symmetric with inflate) + fail-closed on conflict/unresolvable. Fixed in 98ac0c2f, test t/60. Full suite green (4085).
